3. Set up passwordless SSH login from your local Linux system to the remote server by generating an SSH key pair and copying the public key to the remote server.<br><br><em><strong>Constraint:</strong> Do not use a passphrase for the key during this setup.</em>
=>ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 -N ""   # empty passphrase
cat /root/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub > /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
chmod 600 /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
chmod 700 /root/.ssh

4. Simulate a Zomato-style admin task: Write a bash script on your local machine that uses ssh to remotely restart the 'nginx' service on the remote server and then checks its status. Save your script as 'remote_nginx_check.sh'.
=>#!/bin/bash
# Remote nginx restart and status check (Zomato-style admin task)
REMOTE_USER="root"
REMOTE_HOST="localhost"
SSH_KEY="/root/.ssh/id_ed25519"

echo "Connecting to remote server to restart nginx..."
ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -i "$SSH_KEY" ${REMOTE_USER}@${REMOTE_HOST} \
  "service nginx restart 2>/dev/null || systemctl restart nginx 2>/dev/null || echo 'nginx service not found or failed to restart'"

echo "Checking nginx status..."
ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -i "$SSH_KEY" ${REMOTE_USER}@${REMOTE_HOST} \
  "service nginx status 2>/dev/null || systemctl status nginx --no-pager 2>/dev/null || echo 'nginx is not installed or not running'"

5. Find and fix the error in this ssh command: ssh user@192.168.1.100:/home/user/music_downloads<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Review the correct syntax for connecting to a remote server with ssh.</em>
=>ssh user@192.168.1.100:/home/user/music_downloads
Problem:

SSH is only for opening a remote shell (or running a command). The syntax user@host:/path is used by scp or sftp, not by ssh. The colon + path is being misinterpreted.
Correct forms:

Open a shell on the remote server:Bashssh user@192.168.1.100
Run a specific command:Bashssh user@192.168.1.100 "ls /home/user/music_downloads"
Copy a file (use scp instead):Bashscp file.txt user@192.168.1.100:/home/user/music_downloads/
